  "articleBody": "A damaged basement door is more than an eyesore; it is an immediate threat to your home's foundation and finished spaces. Knowing when a sticky latch has turned into a structural or moisture emergency saves thousands in repair bills.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nMinor latch alignment can sometimes be a quick fix, but specific warning signs mean you should bring in an experienced general contractor right away:\n\n- Water pooling near the threshold: Puddles forming after rain indicate failed sill flashing, clogged stair drains, or negative exterior grading directing water against the jamb.\n- Sticking frames from foundation movement: If the door rubs against the frame and masonry shows stair-step cracks, the wall opening may have shifted under structural load.\n- Rotted jambs and framing members: Soft, crumbling wood around the sill shows long-term moisture wick, which destroys framing integrity and invites mold behind drywall.\n- Drafts and visible daylight: Gaps that let in winter air or street runoff signal degraded weatherstripping or warped door slabs that need full unit replacement.\n- Egress non-compliance: If you are converting a basement space into a bedroom or living suite, your door and exterior stairs must satisfy local municipal codes for safe exit dimensions and clearances.\n\nWhen masonry cutting, structural lintels, or persistent water management are involved, DIY efforts usually fall short. HH Remodeling LLC provides hands-on remodeling and carpentry across Aurora and Denver. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your basement door project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
